# Workflows (from Kilo commands)

**Workflow-driven**: commands own the process and embed Skills For Real Engineers thinking and solutions into each step. Because agents may skip skills, **the workflow calls them explicitly**.
Apply the **16 workflows** under `.kilo/commands/` as the same steps in Cursor.

> **Cursor limitations**: slash commands / agents cannot run natively. **Open `@.kilo/commands/<name>.md` and apply the steps manually**, reading `@.kilo/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md` at each step. Roles are in `@.kilo/agents/<role>.md`.
>
> **Call order**: ① select via MCP `capabilities` / `skill_search` (or `@.kilo/CAPABILITIES.md`) → ② `@.kilo/commands/<name>.md` → ③ the skills you need → ④ follow the output schema and gates.

| Workflow | Purpose |
|---|---|
| **`/feature-delivery`** | Deliver a feature through discovery → design → implement → test → review → approval |
| **`/ui-delivery`** | Deliver a UI change through design → implement → accessibility/quality check → approval |
| **`/design-review`** | UI design review (`design-review` → `web-design-guidelines` → `accessibility-audit`) |
| **`/research`** | Research → decision (`research` → `research-decision-room` → `product-discovery` → `to-spec`/`plan-md`) |
| **`/market-plan`** | Market research → strategy → plan (`research` → `research-decision-room` → `product-discovery` → `marketing-psychology` → `plan-md`) |
| **`/compliance-review`** | Legal / privacy / security gate (`compliance-legal` → `privacy-review` → `security-review` → `release-readiness`) |
| **`/release-review`** | Pre-release preparation / check (version, CHANGELOG, legal/NOTICE, deploy, rollback) |
| **`/incident-response`** | Incident: reproduce → isolate → mitigate → permanent fix → retro |
| **`/sprint-plan`** | Sprint planning (`wayfinder` → `to-tickets` → priority/estimate/capacity → `plan-md`) |
| **`/status-report`** | Progress / status report (`triage`/`to-tickets` → progress/risk → `plan-md`) |
| **`/self-review`** | Self-correction (`code-review` → `code-skeptic` → `diagnosing-bugs`/`tdd` → `memory`) |
| **`/self-improve`** | Self-improvement (`retro` → `pdca-cycle` → `plan-md` → `memory`) |
| **`/deck`** | Proposal / planning deck (`research` → `marketing-psychology` → `slides`; pptx optional) |
| **`/writing`** | Creative/article writing (explore → beats → shape): blog, essay, fiction, script drafts (`writing-fragments` → `writing-beats` → `writing-shape`) |

# Agent roles (from Kilo agents)

The 22 roles under `.kilo/agents/`. In Cursor, review/implement "from that role's viewpoint".
- Entry: **wawoo-auto** (default primary agent; ALWAYS route non-trivial work via MCP first)
- Delivery/design/implementation/quality: delivery-lead, project-manager, product-owner, architect, implementer, qa-engineer, data, code-reviewer, code-skeptic, code-simplifier
- Security/ops/release: security-reviewer, compliance-reviewer, performance-reviewer, sre-operator, release-manager
- UI/docs/market: web-designer, frontend-specialist, accessibility-reviewer, docs-specialist, docs-localization-reviewer, market-researcher


## MCP tools (Kilo / Cursor / OpenCode)

`interpret_intent` → `workflow_get` → `skill_get` / `memory_recall` → `delegate_subtask` / `steer_task` → `workflow_clear`.

- Workflows declare `replay: safe|unsafe`; pass `idempotency_key` for `unsafe` steps and re-run only `safe` steps automatically.
- Decomposition (goal → step → verify success → next) is the PM / Delivery Lead supervision loop.

# Gates (required)

- **Approval**: stop and get approval for destructive changes, production, deletions, external transmission, and contracts/terms.
- **Evidence**: commands run, results, screenshots/diff. Distinguish measured from unverified.
- **Observed failure**: base work on failures that actually happened, not inference.
